From 7a9ac77f81b2b27c70b995966899ec14a1597219 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:02:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: airoha: add EN7580 GPHY calibration

EN7580 uses the same 0x03a29491 integrated GPHY ID as EN7528, but its
vendor analog initialization and calibration constants are not
identical. A second PHY driver entry therefore cannot distinguish the
SoCs reliably.

Select the 0x03a29491 calibration profile from the machine compatible
instead. Add the EN7580 MMD and Token Ring initialization, R44 mapping
table, calibration gating, pair-specific ZCAL selection, TX amplitude
compensation, and EN7580 CHIP-SCU RASEL mirror while keeping the
EN7528-specific LDO handling isolated to EN7528.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Samapio Queiroga <me@sirherobrine23.com.br>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
